# Data and assumptions

The local dataset is deterministic (seed 42), numeric and under 10,000 rows. IDs are
stable and unique. Timestamps represent hourly observations. Missing IDs fail;
nonfinite features are dropped. Missing future labels are permitted for scoring.
Remote seed input must be used only once in an isolated DEV catalog.

For classification/regression the observations are independent. Use a group split for
repeated entities and a temporal split for time-dependent outcomes in a real project.
Synthetic accuracy is not evidence of real-world model performance.

Remote training logs the input dataframe's MLflow dataset digest, source table,
row count, source revision and environment versions. The digest identifies the
collected snapshot; archive source Delta versions separately for long-term replay.
Driver collection fails above `--max-rows` (10,000 by default). Replace the trainer
and scoring adapter for larger datasets; the Lakeflow pipeline remains distributed.
